---
title: Scalloped Potatoes and Ham
description: Layers of thinly sliced Yukon Gold potatoes baked in a creamy cheddar sauce until bubbly and golden, served alongside a baked ham.
course: main
cuisine: American
servings: 10
time required: 1 hour 15 minutes
prep time: 15 minutes
cook time: 1 hour
source: https://www.mamaknowsglutenfree.com/gluten-free-scalloped-potatoes/#wprm-recipe-container-11480
image: https://www.mamaknowsglutenfree.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/featured-gluten-free-scalloped-potatoes-recipe-1.jpg
tags:
  - potatoes
  - ham
  - casserole
  - comfort food
  - gluten free
---

Preheat the #oven{} to 400F. Grease a #9x13 baking dish{} with cooking spray.

Melt @unsalted butter{4%tbsp} in a #medium saucepan{} over medium-high heat. Add @whole milk{2%cups} and whisk to combine.

Whisk in @gluten-free all-purpose flour{1/4%cup}, then stir in @salt{1.5%tsp}, @black pepper{1/4%tsp}, @onion powder{1%tbsp}, @garlic powder{1%tbsp}, and @dried thyme{1%tsp}.

Add @chicken broth{1%cup} and whisk. Cook for ~saucepan{2%minutes} until it just begins to simmer around the edges and thickens, then remove from heat.

Spread half of the @Yukon Gold potatoes{4%lbs}(sliced 1/4-inch thick) evenly in the greased baking dish. Top with half the cream sauce.

Sprinkle @shredded Parmesan cheese{1/2%cup} and @shredded cheddar cheese{1%cup} over the layer.

Add the remaining potatoes, the remaining sauce, and the remaining @shredded cheddar cheese{1%cup}.

Cover with foil and bake for ~oven{30%minutes}. Remove the foil and bake uncovered for another ~oven{30%minutes}, until the potatoes are cooked through and the top is golden.

Let cool a few minutes before serving warm.

> Note: Cook a ham alongside the potatoes and serve the two together.
